From d3f1ff606854af3c10ddcda54ece6fc1aa614e22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Collins Lu <collins_lu@sertek.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:08:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] smart-intersection: start dlstreamer pipelines sequentially,
 fix node-red build

dlstreamer-pipeline-server's built-in auto_start launches all 4 camera
pipelines concurrently right as it finishes booting, which reliably
crashes every one of them (the gvapython datapublisher callback races
to open an MQTT connection at the same instant). Disable auto_start in
config.json and add a one-shot dlstreamer-pipeline-starter container
that starts them sequentially over the REST API instead, surviving
restarts/reboots.

Also switch node-red to build from a local Dockerfile that installs
node-red-contrib-influxdb at image build time, instead of installing
it at container startup via install_package.sh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../compose-scenescape.yml                    |   29 +-
 .../dlstreamer-pipeline-server/config.json    | 1640 ++++++++---------
 .../start_pipelines.py                        |   76 +
 .../src/node-red/Dockerfile                   |    4 +
 4 files changed, 926 insertions(+), 823 deletions(-)
